summary:
  When a cast ends, the record of who refused the station goes with it.

history:
  A device that refuses stays ticked, and its row in the output menu now
  says "Cannot play this station" until it is asked again or unticked. The
  one device refusing is what ends the cast, so a record emptied at the end
  would take the mark down in the very moment it was put up: the Ruark's
  row would never show it when the Ruark is the only device.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CastLogic.js

find:
      out.refused = _copy(session).refused;

replace:
      out.refused = {};

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_castlogic.qml::test_the_end_of_a_cast_keeps_the_marks_and_nothing_else.
